    We then utilized the Poisson binomial distribution combined with Monte Carlo simulations
to estimate the expected number of countries likely to win their first Olympic medal and their
confidence intervals. The simulation results, shown in Figure 9, indicate that the probability is
highest when the number of first-time medal-winning countries is exactly 3.




                                   Figure 9: Monte Carlo Simulation of First-Time Medal-Winning Countries


    Based on these findings, we conclude that 3 countries are the most likely to win their first
Olympic medal in the next Games.The simulation results align well with our predictions, con-
firming the robustness of the model’s estimates. The Monte Carlo simulation not only validated
the expected outcomes but also provided a probabilistic range for the number of countries likely
to win their first medal in the next Olympics.
